body:
### User Story
When CoreDNS is doing domain name resolution, if it encounters an unknown domain name, CoreDNS will return an `NXDOMAIN` error.  But the default behavior for `resolv.conf` will only try the next nameserver if the first nameserver times out or it receives a SERVFAIL from the first nameserver. 

I found that the Template plugin can accomplish a similar effect. But Template has no way to filter the return code. For example, I just want to redefine the error code of `NXDOMAIN` as `SERVFAIL`. 

```yaml
    .:53 {
        template ANY ANY {
          rcode SERVFAIL
        }
    }
```

So I would like to ask, is there any other way to do it? Or the Template plugin needs to support similar functions? In addition, the Template plugin is executed before the Forward plugin. So there is no way to redefine the return code of the Forward plugin.
